.TH "CSSNUMERICVALUE.DIV" "3JS" "August 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSNumericValue.div \- CSSNumericValue: div() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]div()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R]
interface divides the \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] by the supplied value.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
div()
div(number1)
div(number1, number2)
div(number1, number2, /* \&..., */ numberN)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]number1\f[R], \&..., \f[B]numberN\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
Either a number or a \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R].
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]CSSMathProduct\f[R], or a \f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] if
\f[CR]this\f[R] and every argument are plain numbers, or all but one of
them are.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Thrown if an invalid type was passed to the method.
.TP
\f[B]RangeError\f[R]
Thrown if any of \f[CR]number1\f[R], \&..., \f[CR]numberN\f[R] is, or
resolves to, 0 or \-0.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
.IP
.EX
\f[B]let\f[R] mathProduct = CSS.px(24).div(CSS.percent(4));
\f[I]// Prints \(dqcalc(24px / 4%)\(dq\f[R]
mathProduct.toString();
.EE
